2. Logical Architecture
2.1 User Interface Layer
Purpose: Provide intuitive web-based interface for users to interact with the IMS Components:
2.1.1 Web Application (SPA - Single Page Application)
Technology: React
Characteristics:
Responsive design (desktop, tablet, mobile)
Rich user experience with minimal page reloads
Real-time data updates via WebSocket or polling
Client-side validation and error handling

Key Screens:
Dashboard (inventory overview, alerts, KPIs)
Inventory Management (search, view, adjust)
Purchase Order Management (create, approve, track)
Forecasting & Replenishment (recommendations, overrides)
Reporting & Analytics (generate, export)
Admin Console (user management, configuration)

2.1.2 Mobile Experience (Future Enhancement)
Mobile-optimized responsive design
Progressive Web App (PWA) for offline capability
Barcode scanning for warehouse operations
2.2 Application Services Layer
Purpose: Expose business functionality via RESTful APIs; orchestrate business logic 
Components:
2.2.1 Inventory Management Service Responsibilities:
Manage inventory master data (SKUs, locations, quantities)
Process stock-in and stock-out transactions
Handle inventory adjustments
Track lot/batch and expiry dates
Enforce inventory business rules
Key APIs:
GET /api/inventory - Retrieve inventory levels
GET /api/inventory/{sku} - Get SKU details
POST /api/inventory/adjust - Create adjustment
GET /api/inventory/expiring - Get expiring inventory
POST /api/inventory/transfer - Create transfer
2.2.2 Forecasting & Demand Planning Service Responsibilities:
Analyze historical sales data
Generate demand forecasts
Detect seasonality and trends
Apply promotional adjustments
Calculate reorder points
Key APIs:
GET /api/forecasts/{sku} - Get forecast for SKU
POST /api/forecasts/generate - Trigger forecast generation
PUT /api/forecasts/{sku} - Override forecast
GET /api/forecasts/accuracy - Get forecast accuracy metrics

2.2.3 Purchase Order Management Service Responsibilities:
Create and manage purchase orders
Validate supplier requirements (MOQ, case pack)
Manage PO approval workflow
Track PO status and receipts
Generate PO recommendations
Key APIs:
GET /api/purchase-orders - List POs
POST /api/purchase-orders - Create PO
PUT /api/purchase-orders/{id}/approve - Approve PO
POST /api/purchase-orders/{id}/receive - Record receipt
GET /api/recommendations/replenishment - Get replenishment recommendations
2.2.4 Reporting & Analytics Service
Responsibilities:
Generate standard reports
Provide dashboard data
Support ad-hoc queries
Export reports to Excel/PDF
Calculate KPIs
Key APIs:
GET /api/reports/current-inventory - Current inventory report
GET /api/reports/valuation - Inventory valuation
GET /api/reports/variance - Reconciliation variance report
GET /api/dashboard/summary - Dashboard KPIs
POST /api/reports/export - Export report
2.2.5 User Management Service Responsibilities:
Authenticate users
Manage user accounts
Enforce role-based access control
Handle session management


Key APIs:
POST /api/auth/login - User login
POST /api/auth/logout - User logout
GET /api/users - List users
POST /api/users - Create user
PUT /api/users/{id}/roles - Update user roles
2.2.6 Integration Gateway Service Responsibilities:
		Route requests to external systems
Handle authentication for external APIs
Implement retry logic and error handling
Log integration activity
Throttle requests to respect rate limits
Key Functions:
QuickBooks integration orchestration
WMS integration orchestration
Sales channel integration orchestration
Webhook handling for real-time events
2.3 Business Logic Layer
Purpose: Implement core business rules and algorithms; ensure data integrity Components:
2.3.1 Inventory Business Rules Engine Rules Implemented:
FEFO allocation logic
Negative inventory prevention
Regional SKU availability enforcement
