5.2.3 Session Management
Session timeout: 30 minutes of inactivity
Secure session tokens (HTTP-only, Secure flag)
Session invalidation on logout
Concurrent session limit: 3 per user
5.3 Data Encryption
5.3.1 Data in Transit
Protocol: TLS 1.2 or higher
Certificates: SSL/TLS certificates from trusted CA
All API Communication: HTTPS only
Database Connections: Encrypted connections
5.3.2 Data at Rest
Database: AWS RDS encryption enabled (AES-256)
File Storage: S3 bucket encryption (AES-256)
Backups: Encrypted backups
Key Management: AWS KMS (Key Management Service)
5.4 API Security
5.4.1 Authentication
Internal APIs: JWT (JSON Web Token) with short expiration
External APIs: API keys or OAuth 2.0
5.4.2 Rate Limiting
Prevent abuse and DDoS attacks
Limit: 100 requests per minute per user
Throttling for exceeding limits
5.4.3 Input Validation
Validate all input parameters
Sanitize input to prevent injection attacks
Use parameterized queries for database access
