6.3 Database Design Principles
Normalization: 3NF (Third Normal Form) to reduce redundancy
Referential Integrity: Foreign key constraints enforced
Indexing Strategy: Indexes on frequently queried columns (SKU, ProductID, WarehouseID, dates)
Audit Trail: Timestamps (CreatedDate, ModifiedDate) on all tables
Soft Deletes: Use IsActive flags instead of hard deletes where appropriate
Historical Data: Retain historical records for forecasting and analytics

7. Technology Stack Recommendations
7.1 Frontend
Recommended: React.js 
Justification:
Modern, widely-adopted JavaScript frameworks
Rich ecosystem and community support
Component-based architecture for maintainability
Excellent performance and user experience
Additional Libraries:
UI Framework: Material-UI, Ant Design, or Bootstrap for consistent design
State Management: Redux 
Charts/Graphs: Chart.js or D3.js for reporting visualizations
